WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:15.464
"Ready?" Sujong asked.

2
00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:19.707
She was Nina's after-school guest today at Kids Central.

3
00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:22.590
"Ready!" Nina said.

4
00:00:23.551 --> 00:00:25.892
Her backpack was filled with special ingredients.

5
00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:30.136
"I hope everyone likes Korean food," she thought.

6
00:00:35.316 --> 00:00:35.596
"Aunt Sujong!"

7
00:00:35.616 --> 00:00:36.197
Izzie cried.

8
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:38.478
"Welcome back!"

9
00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:39.899
Miss Shelly smiled.

10
00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:42.001
"It's so nice to see you."

11
00:00:42.021 --> 00:00:44.683
"Are you going to play soccer with us?"

12
00:00:45.063 --> 00:00:45.824
Bobby asked.

13
00:00:46.844 --> 00:00:47.565
Nina blinked.

14
00:00:47.585 --> 00:00:55.071
"Actually," she said softly, "we are going to show you how to make Korean food."

15
00:00:55.091 --> 00:00:58.193
"Does everyone here like chicken?"

16
00:00:58.593 --> 00:01:00.354
Aunt Sujong asked cheerfully.

17
00:01:00.374 --> 00:01:06.486
"Yes!" "Then I think you'll like this recipe."

18
00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.288
Aunt Sujong took out a list of ingredients.

19
00:01:09.308 --> 00:01:12.851
"Nina, can you read this aloud for your friends?"

20
00:01:15.073 --> 00:01:15.954
Nina swallowed.

21
00:01:17.215 --> 00:01:19.317
A couple of ingredients had Korean names.

22
00:01:19.337 --> 00:01:23.540
"Cheongju." "What's that?"

23
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:24.601
Ethan asked.

24
00:01:24.621 --> 00:01:28.204
"It's rice wine," Aunt Sujong answered.

25
00:01:28.224 --> 00:01:30.646
"We use it often in Korean cooking.

26
00:01:31.246 --> 00:01:32.908
I'm glad you're asking questions."

27
00:01:34.064 --> 00:01:35.004
Nina kept reading.

28
00:01:35.725 --> 00:01:36.745
"Salt and pepper.

29
00:01:37.245 --> 00:01:38.866
Chicken. Mushrooms.

30
00:01:39.406 --> 00:01:40.306
Green onions.

31
00:01:40.926 --> 00:01:42.206
Cooking oil spray.

32
00:01:42.787 --> 00:01:44.927
Ketchup. Sesame oil.

33
00:01:45.447 --> 00:01:46.188
Soy sauce.

34
00:01:46.848 --> 00:01:48.968
Honey." She paused.

35
00:01:48.988 --> 00:01:52.209
"And gochujang."

36
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.890
"Go-what?" Bobby asked.

37
00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:59.171
"Gochujang," Aunt Sujong said.

38
00:01:59.191 --> 00:02:01.172
"It's a red pepper paste."

39
00:02:02.316 --> 00:02:03.657
"Let's get started!"

40
00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:04.537
Bobby said.

41
00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:10.340
"First, we'll make two sauces," Aunt Sujong said.

42
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.901
"We'll marinate the chicken in one sauce.

43
00:02:13.761 --> 00:02:18.023
Then we'll brush a gochujang sauce onto the chicken while it cooks."

44
00:02:19.964 --> 00:02:23.646
Aunt Sujong helped the girls cut the chicken, mushrooms, and green onions.

45
00:02:25.287 --> 00:02:27.348
Miss Shelly helped the boys mix the sauces.

46
00:02:29.136 --> 00:02:35.880
Ethan and Bobby mixed ketchup, gochujang, honey, soy sauce, sesame oil, and garlic into a bowl.

47
00:02:38.201 --> 00:02:41.723
Jason poured cheongju into another bowl for the marinade.

48
00:02:42.384 --> 00:02:44.225
Then he sprinkled in some salt and pepper.

49
00:02:44.245 --> 00:02:47.166
"The marinade is ready!"

50
00:02:47.507 --> 00:02:48.267
Jason said.

51
00:02:49.648 --> 00:02:53.050
The girls poured the marinade onto the chicken and covered it in plastic.

52
00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.412
Then they sprinkled salt on the green onions and mushrooms.

53
00:02:57.956 --> 00:02:59.296
"Great job, everyone.

54
00:03:00.117 --> 00:03:02.797
Let's take a hike while the chicken marinates.

55
00:03:03.798 --> 00:03:07.779
When we get back, everything will be ready," Miss Shelly said.

56
00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.921
After the hike everyone washed their hands.

57
00:03:15.681 --> 00:03:17.382
Aunt Sujong handed out skewers.

58
00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:21.203
"You each get to make your own skewer."

59
00:03:22.563 --> 00:03:24.324
Everyone watched as Nina made hers.

60
00:03:25.916 --> 00:03:28.337
She carefully put one piece of chicken on the skewer.

61
00:03:29.418 --> 00:03:30.138
Then a mushroom.

62
00:03:30.938 --> 00:03:32.159
Then a piece of green onion.

63
00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:34.980
She repeated until her skewer was full.

64
00:03:36.441 --> 00:03:38.061
Nina's friends made their skewers.

65
00:03:39.862 --> 00:03:42.363
Miss Shelly sprayed cooking oil on an electric grill.

66
00:03:42.383 --> 00:03:44.504
"The grill is ready!"

67
00:03:46.045 --> 00:03:47.886
Everyone placed their skewers on the grill.

68
00:03:49.927 --> 00:03:52.428
Jason brushed on the gochujang sauce.

69
00:03:54.668 --> 00:03:56.209
"Be careful when you brush!"

70
00:03:56.809 --> 00:03:57.829
Aunt Sujong said.

71
00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:03.792
After a few minutes, they turned the skewers over and brushed on more sauce.

72
00:04:09.914 --> 00:04:11.015
they be ready soon?"

73
00:04:11.475 --> 00:04:12.135
Izzie asked.

74
00:04:12.155 --> 00:04:16.997
"We have to make sure the chicken is fully cooked," Nina said.

75
00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.538
Soon the skewers were ready.

76
00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:22.599
Ethan took a bite.

77
00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.544
"Spicy. And yummy!"

78
00:04:30.066 --> 00:04:31.207
"Too spicy!"

79
00:04:31.827 --> 00:04:32.607
Jason said.

80
00:04:32.627 --> 00:04:37.149
"Try putting on some ketchup," Nina offered.

81
00:04:41.851 --> 00:04:44.032
Less spicy and more delicious!”

82
00:04:44.552 --> 00:04:45.552
Jason smiled.

83
00:04:45.572 --> 00:04:50.314
"These are so good," Izzie said.

84
00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:54.156
"I want to try more Korean food," Bobby said.

85
00:04:55.305 --> 00:04:56.107
Nina beamed.

86
00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.097
Her friends seemed to love this Korean food.

87
00:04:59.979 --> 00:05:02.327
And that made her own chicken taste even better!
